Minimal shielded pool — a BN254 / Groth16 shielded pool for Ethereum

Original sources (the circuit, the pool contract and the dispatcher in core/,
the client in sdk/, the tests and the tools) are licensed under Apache-2.0 (see
LICENSE).

This project builds on:

  iden3/circomlib 2.0.5 and iden3/circomlibjs 0.1.7 (GPL-3.0): the spend
  circuit includes circomlib's poseidon.circom and bitify.circom at compile
  time (fetched via npm, not vendored), and
  sdk/poseidon_bn254_constants.json plus
  test/vectors/poseidon_bn254_vectors.json are exported from circomlibjs by
  tools/export_vectors.js. core/contracts/src/PoseidonBN254.sol and the split
  PoseidonT3.sol / PoseidonT4.sol are generated from those constants.

  iden3/snarkjs 0.7.5 (GPL-3.0): core/contracts/src/Groth16Verifier.sol is
  generated by snarkjs's `zkey export solidityverifier` from this circuit's
  proving key and carries its GPL-3.0 header. It has been modified since July
  2026: tools/patch_verifier.py gives its three precompile calls a fixed 500,000
  gas request instead of reading gas() and, since August 2026, adds checks that
  reject non-canonical proof coordinates and points at infinity.

sdk/frametx.py derives from lambdaclass/ethrex's reference type-0x06
frame-transaction encoder for the Hegotá devnet (scripts/hegota-devnet/frametx.py,
hegota-devnet branch) and has since been adapted to the current EIP-8141
envelope. ethrex is Apache-2.0 / MIT dual-licensed. sdk/pool_frametx.py and
evidence/REVIEW.md are original Apache-2.0 work.
